@ignore
Feature: Semi-Integration
  As an Admin,
  I want to control the semi-integration functionalities,
  So that I can manage different configurations.

  @ignore
  Scenario 1: Deactivate semi-integration and verify terminal info
    Given Aureliano is managing the semi-integration settings,
    When he deactivates the semi-integration feature,
    Then he should see in the terminal’s information that semi-integration is not active.

  @ignore
  Scenario 2: Activate semi-integration without password prompt and verify terminal info.
    Given Aureliano is managing the semi-integration settings,
    When he activates the semi-integration feature but leaves the password prompt off,
    Then he should see that the terminal indicates semi-integration is active,
    And he should see that no idle screen after waiting 30 seconds on the Main Screen.

  @ignore
  Scenario 3: Activate semi-integration without password prompt and verify terminal info.
    Given Aureliano is managing the semi-integration settings,
    When he activates the semi-integration feature and the password prompt,
    Then he should see that the terminal indicates semi-integration is active,
    And he should see that the idle screen after waiting 30 seconds on the Main Screen.

  @ignore
  Scenario 4: Log-In to Standalone Mode.
    Given Aureliano is in the Semi-Integration Idle Screen,
    When he logged-in to Standalone Mode with ID 1 and password 111111,
    Then he should see the Main screen.

  @ignore
  Scenario 4: Activate semi-integration with password prompt to validate only Admin can access to Standalone Mode.
    Given Aureliano is either logged in Standalone Mode or managing the semi-integration settings,
    And he removes all clerks except himself (ID 1),
    And he attempts to add multiple clerks with the following data:
      | Alias      | Clerk ID | Role     | Password |
      #| Aureliano  | 1       | Admin  | 111111   |
      | Melquiades | 22       | Manager  | 222222   |
      | Eusebia    | 33       | Employee | 333333   |
    When he activates the semi-integration feature and the password prompt,
    Then he should see that the terminal indicates semi-integration is active,
    And he should see that the password prompt is required after 30 seconds,
    And he should see that Melquiades and Eusebia cannot access to Standalone Mode.

  @ignore
  Scenario 5: Log in and wait 30 seconds on the main screen to check if the password prompt returns.
    Given Aureliano is either logged in Standalone Mode or managing the semi-integration settings,
    When he waits for 30 seconds on the main screen,
    Then he should see that the password prompt is required after 30 seconds.

  @ignore
  Scenario 6: Deactivate semi-integration and password features, then check terminal info.
    Given Aureliano is either logged in Standalone Mode or managing the semi-integration settings,
    When he turns off the semi-integration feature and the password requirement,
    Then he should confirm in the terminal info that semi-integration is inactive,
    And he should see that the password prompt is no required after 30 seconds.

  @ignore
  Scenario 7: Deactivate semi-integration and activate the password prompt, then verify that the configuration is invalid for a time-based prompt.
    Given Aureliano is managing the semi-integration settings,
    When Aureliano sets semi-integration to off but activates the password prompt,
    Then he should confirm in the terminal info that semi-integration is inactive,
    And he should see that the password prompt is no required after 30 seconds.
